 ## Honest ceiling
 
-AnonSync is still not a production peer discovery system, encrypted peer protocol, persisted transfer scheduler, file watcher, daemon, UI, invite/share-key authority, or deployable privacy-preserving distributed sync product. Rev0679 verifies that terminal checkpoint evidence still matches both current source and destination filesystem roots, but it does not replay checkpoint rows into resumed work, persist in-flight request/schedule/batch state before crash, own abandoned transfers, model tombstone/conflict branches inside the fake session, or define peer/folder trust as non-caller-authored authority. The next durable product move is actionable non-terminal restart: reconstruct pending staged transfers from SQLite plus source/destination/staging filesystem inspection, persist request and peer-schedule rows before each transfer round, and record cleanup transitions before and after filesystem mutation.
+AnonSync is still not a production peer discovery system, encrypted peer protocol, persisted transfer scheduler, file watcher, daemon, UI, invite/share-key authority, or deployable privacy-preserving distributed sync product. Rev0680 verifies that terminal checkpoint evidence still matches source, destination, and staging cleanup truth, but it does not replay checkpoint rows into resumed work, persist in-flight request/schedule/batch state before crash, own abandoned transfers, model tombstone/conflict branches inside the fake session, or define peer/folder trust as non-caller-authored authority. The next durable product move is executable restart planning: reconstruct pending staged transfers from SQLite plus source/destination/staging filesystem inspection, then persist request and peer-schedule rows before each transfer round.
