+-# AnonSync slim C++ working cube — rev0679
++# AnonSync slim C++ working cube — rev0680
+ 
+ AnonSync is a **C++ peer-to-peer file synchronization system**. The product target is Resilio Sync-style local folder replication across authorized devices: discover or address peers, compare authenticated file manifests, transfer missing content-addressed chunks, apply creates/updates/deletes exactly once, preserve conflicts honestly, and resume after interruption without a central service being the ordinary source of truth.
+ 
+-Rev0679 is code-bearing. It promotes the active executable to:
++Rev0680 is code-bearing. It promotes the active executable to:
+ 
+-- `bin/rev0679/anonsync_core-linux-x86_64-gcc-openssl3-sqlite3`
++- `bin/rev0680/anonsync_core-linux-x86_64-gcc-openssl3-sqlite3`
+ 
+-The active C++ slice is now a **source filesystem resume probe** plus a small audit/refactor of the rev0678 destination-only checker. Rev0678 made completed checkpoint resume views prove durable SQLite integrity, exact chunk coverage, and current destination-tree agreement. Rev0679 makes the restart reader symmetric: by default, terminal session evidence now also requires the current `source_root_path` to match the persisted `source` manifest by path, kind, size, and SHA-256.
++The active C++ slice is now a **staging cleanup resume probe**. Rev0678 and rev0679 made the completed checkpoint resume view verify current destination and source filesystem truth. Rev0680 adds the missing third local surface: the staging root. A terminal checkpoint is trusted by default only when committed staged-transfer artifacts are actually absent from `staging_root_path`, not merely marked cleaned in SQLite.
+ 
+ ## Active sync mission
+ 
+@@ -14,48 +14,47 @@
+ 
+ > Make authorized devices converge on the same intended folder tree without treating a central service as the ordinary source of truth, while preserving enough evidence to recover safely, reject stale or forged work, and expose conflicts honestly.
+ 
+-Rev0679 is not a full restartable scheduler. It hardens the completed checkpoint reader so a restart process does not merely accept a coherent database and a coherent destination tree. With `require_source_filesystem_match` and `require_destination_filesystem_match` both enabled by default, `terminal_session_complete` now requires exact durable checkpoint integrity plus current source and destination files that still match the persisted source and destination-after manifests.
++Rev0680 is still not a full restart executor. It hardens the completed checkpoint reader so a restart process does not accept a coherent database, coherent source tree, and coherent destination tree while stale `.part` files or `.part.chunks` receipt directories remain under the staging root. With `require_staging_artifacts_cleaned`, `require_source_filesystem_match`, and `require_destination_filesystem_match` enabled by default, `terminal_session_complete` now binds durable checkpoint rows, live source bytes, live destination bytes, and live staging cleanup state.
+ 
