-## Rev0679 behavior added
+## Rev0680 behavior added
 
-`load_sync_session_checkpoint_resume_view` now treats a completed checkpoint as terminal only when durable SQLite evidence, exact source chunk coverage, the current source filesystem, and the current destination filesystem agree. The new `require_source_filesystem_match` option defaults to true. When enabled, the reader walks the persisted `source` manifest entries, resolves each path under `source_root_path`, rejects symlink-ancestor substitution, requires file entries to be regular files, hashes their current bytes, and compares size plus SHA-256 against the persisted manifest row. Tombstone rows are treated as absent-path expectations.
+`load_sync_session_checkpoint_resume_view` now treats a completed checkpoint as terminal only when committed staging artifacts are absent from the configured `staging_root_path`. The new `require_staging_artifacts_cleaned` option defaults to true. When enabled, the reader reconstructs every expected cleaned staging path from `sync_session_file_results`, `sync_session_apply_intents`, and the persisted source manifest entry digest, then verifies that the `.part` file and `.part.chunks` receipt directory are gone.
 
-Rev0679 also refactors the rev0678 destination checker into `SyncManifestFilesystemProbe` / `verify_manifest_filesystem_or_throw`, shared by `source` and `destination_after` roles. The resume result now exposes `source_filesystem_verified`, `source_filesystem_entries_checked`, `source_filesystem_file_entries_checked`, `source_filesystem_tombstone_entries_checked`, `source_filesystem_missing_paths`, `source_filesystem_kind_mismatches`, `source_filesystem_content_mismatches`, and `source_filesystem_drift_paths`, alongside the destination fields from rev0678.
+The resume result now exposes `staging_artifacts_verified`, `staging_artifact_paths_checked`, `staging_files_present`, `staging_receipt_directories_present`, `staging_artifact_kind_mismatches`, and bounded `staging_artifact_paths`. This keeps durable cleanup rows separate from current staging-root truth while requiring both by default.
 
-The durable checkpoint schema remains `rev0677-sync-session-checkpoint-v2`; rev0679 changes read-time restart semantics rather than the SQLite row layout. The selftest mutates `docs/session-report.txt` in the source root after checkpoint commit and verifies that strict resume loading rejects the terminal checkpoint. It also verifies advisory mode with `require_source_filesystem_match=false`, where the view loads while reporting one source content mismatch and the drift path.
+The durable checkpoint schema remains `rev0677-sync-session-checkpoint-v2`; rev0680 changes read-time restart semantics rather than the SQLite row layout. The selftest recreates the receipt directory for `docs/session-report.txt` after checkpoint commit and verifies that strict resume loading rejects the terminal checkpoint. It also verifies advisory mode with `require_staging_artifacts_cleaned=false`, where the view loads while reporting one stale receipt directory path.
 
