-The resume view is restart input, not restart execution. It verifies completed checkpoint coherence and current source/destination filesystem truth, but it does not reconstruct transfer rounds, persist in-flight request/schedule/batch state before every crash point, clean abandoned `.part` or `.chunks` state, authenticate transport messages, or encode peer/folder membership authority. It deliberately reports terminal and pending state without mutating the filesystem.
+The resume view is restart input, not restart execution. It verifies completed checkpoint coherence and current source/destination/staging cleanup truth, but it does not reconstruct transfer rounds, persist in-flight request/schedule/batch state before every crash point, clean abandoned unowned `.part` or `.chunks` state, authenticate transport messages, or encode peer/folder membership authority. It deliberately reports terminal and pending state without mutating the filesystem.
